po"><addressbook><name>AOYAMA MASAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OBARA HEITARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA HIDEKATSU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AOYAMA, MASAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OBARA, HEITARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA, HIDEKATSU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Drugs or reagents containing as the active ingredient N-acyloxylated cycloalkyl compounds represented by general formula (I): (wherein A is optionally substituted C4-C5 cycloalkyl which may have one double bond in the ring; and R is C1-C3 alkyl or phenyl).  The above compounds are hydroxyamine derivatives functioning as spin trapping agents and can rapidly react with free radicals or active oxygen in an objective organ in spite of their being excellent in stability during the preparation or administration thereof.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur des médicaments ou réactifs contenant comme ingrédients actifs des composés cycloalkyl N-acyloxylés représentés par la formule générale (I) dans laquelle A représente un C4-C5 cycloalkyl éventuellement substitué qui peut être une double liaison dans le noyau; et R représente un C1-C3 alkyl ou phényl. Les composés précités sont des dérivés d'hydroxyamine agissant comme agent de capture du spin et pouvant rapidement réagir avec des radicaux libres ou l'oxygène actif dans un organe cible en dépit de leur excellente stabilité lors de leur préparation ou de leur administration.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>